{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["people_table:write"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"description":"Write a job\u2019s People table custom cells: action=batch writes 1-500 cells at expectedVersion (people_table.cells.batch), atomic by default (all or nothing) or mode=independent (each edit commits on its own; retrying with the same idempotencyKey finishes only the edits that had not committed), with one result per edit; dryRun=true checks every edit and writes nothing. action=set writes or clears (value null) one cell (people_table.cells.set). Address rows by jobPersonId; a row this key cannot reach is a 404. A PERSON value is a jobPersonId on the same job. Only custom columns are editable (custom:<fieldId>); built-in and system columns answer COLUMN_NOT_EDITABLE. Writes go through the web\u2019s own column and cell rules, at expectedVersion (a stale version is VERSION_MISMATCH), and every audit event records an agent actor and the request\u2019s batchId. Writes spend the key\u2019s write budget (60 requests a minute and 10,000 edits an hour across jobs and surfaces; a dryRun counts as a read). Requires people_table:write, except columns action=list (people_table:read).","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"enum":["batch","set"],"type":"string"},"columnId":{"$ref":"#/properties/edits/items/properties/columnId","description":"set: the custom column."},"dryRun":{"description":"batch: check every edit, write nothing.","type":"boolean"},"edits":{"description":"batch: 1-500 edits, each cell at most once.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"columnId":{"pattern":"^(?:[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}|custom:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64})$","type":"string"},"expectedVersion":{"anyOf":[{"exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Exactly the version read: null only for a never_set cell."},"jobPersonId":{"$ref":"#/properties/jobId"},"va